## Removal and destroy

Removing this resource relinquishes only Terraform's local state binding. It does not delete or retire the Agent Definition, change the running Agent, roll back a Release, or remove immutable Versions, Releases, Configuration Revisions, or audit evidence.

Terraform backend locking coordinates writers that share one state. Separate states have no cross-state lock; binding the same Agent Definition into two roots is an operational error, and later authorized writers appear as drift.
